; THE OTHER HALF OF block/copy16; sixteen staged bytes handed back UP 869
; cells  to the source they were taken from; Entered where the STAGE begins
; and it leaves the pointer on the stage's last cell;
;
; IT LEAVES THE STAGE EMPTY  which is the part that matters to the caller: the
; staging cells of aes/ctr128 are cells the CIPHER uses as workspace  the
; schedule's at 16 and the round key's at 98  and the cipher is entered
; immediately afterwards; So this is not tidiness; a byte left behind here is
; a wrong round key three hundred instructions later;
;
; Every move in it is relative  for the reason block/copy16 records;
; ASSERT ptr=+0
  [-R869+L869]
